<section>
  <p class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "guides", label_type: :nav, class: "cta" %></p>
  <h1>Two controls, and nothing to learn twice.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A pad and a button for the menus, with diagnostic pages for the workbench.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3 id="two-contacts">The pad moves, <span class="highlight">the button acts</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        Two controls, with one role each to remember.
        The capacitive touch pad on the top edge cycles through the four pages,
        without changing settings. The button on the side opens the current page&rsquo;s menu,
        and each further press changes the value in the selected row.
      </p>
      <p>
        Two pages have a menu. All the settings you can change with the controls are in the radar menu,
        the first screen used to set up the device. No change needs confirming:
        each press applies the change immediately.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-radar.png", alt: "The radar menu: aircraft type, callsign, units, range, plot, alarm and volume, with the hint PAD MOVES - BUTTON CHANGES at the bottom" %>
      <figcaption>The radar menu</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <ul class="points">
    <li>Tap the pad to go to the next page</li>
    <li>Touch the pad for a second to return to the radar</li>
    <li>Press the button to open the menu, if the page has one</li>
    <li>Press again to change the value in the selected row</li>
    <li>Move past the last row to return to the page</li>
    <li>Leave the controls untouched for a minute to return to the page automatically</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <h3 id="callsign">Your callsign, <span class="highlight">entered with two controls</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        <span class="mono">CALLSIGN</span> is the only row that opens an entry field
        instead of changing a value. Inside it, the controls swap roles:
        the pad changes the character above the bar, and the button moves to the
        next character. The cycle runs from a blank to a dash, <span class="mono">A</span> to
        <span class="mono">Z</span>, <span class="mono">0</span> to
        <span class="mono">9</span>, then back to the blank. If you pass a letter,
        keep cycling to reach it again with the same gesture.
      </p>
      <p>
        Press the button on the last character to save the callsign. Any blanks
        at the end are removed. To clear a callsign, change the first
        character to a blank and press the button. The screen says
        <span class="mono">BLANK THE FIRST TO CLEAR</span> while a callsign is
        present, and <span class="mono">BUTTON CLEARS</span> once the blank is
        under the bar. If you leave the field before finishing, or leave it untouched for a
        minute, nothing is saved.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-callsign.png", alt: "The callsign field: S-BLIP at triple height, a bar under the third character, PAD ROLLS above BUTTON NEXT, and BLANK THE FIRST TO CLEAR along the bottom" %>
      <figcaption>The callsign field</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="shots">
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-callsign-blank.png", alt: "The callsign field with the first character changed to a blank, the bar under it, and the hint now reading PAD ROLLS above BUTTON CLEARS" %>
      <figcaption>The first character blanked</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-callsign-none.png", alt: "The radar menu after the press, with the CALLSIGN row selected and reading NONE" %>
      <figcaption>One press later</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <h3 id="diagnostics">Four pages to cycle through, <span class="highlight">the rest by name</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        Tapping cycles through the radar, the list, the instruments, then the
        g-meter, and no other pages. A pilot cycling through pages in flight should
        not end up on the satellite bars. A board with no inertial sensor has no
        g-meter to display, so tapping skips that page rather than showing
        <span class="mono">NO SENSOR</span> every fourth time.
      </p>
      <p>
        Open the other pages by name from the list&rsquo;s menu. When you close them,
        you return to the page you were on. The screens below are for the workbench,
        the apron and bug reports. You cannot reach them by cycling through
        pages with the pad. The last one records a flight for a bug report:
        all data categories for a bug, or only power and duty for a discharge test. It
        shows how much flash memory the selected recording will use before you start.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "menu-nearby.png", alt: "The nearby menu: status, satellites, radio log, raw data, capture and self test, the six pages opened by name" %>
      <figcaption>The list&rsquo;s menu</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="shots">
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "status.png", alt: "The status page: position fix and satellites, position, track, traffic count, transmit state, the sensor hub, pressure, the two altitudes, speed, vertical speed, and the battery in volts and percent" %>
      <figcaption>Status</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "satellites.png", alt: "The satellites page: one bar per satellite grouped by constellation, with a dotted reference line at 40 dB-Hz" %>
      <figcaption>Satellites</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "radio-log.png", alt: "The radio log: below the position fix, the pulse-per-second (PPS) signal state and the background noise level, one row per short radio transmission received or sent, newest first, with its time, direction, channel, contents, address and signal level" %>
      <figcaption>Radio log</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "self-test.png", alt: "The self test page: one row per part of the board, each showing which part responded and its test result" %>
      <figcaption>Self test</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "capture.png", alt: "The capture page with no recording in progress: the state is off, with two recording types to choose from, FULL for all data categories and POWER RUN for power and duty. It shows the cost of the selected type: the sectors of flash memory it would use, the stored flights it would delete and the hours of recording it would retain, with PAD PICKS, PRESS TWICE TO ARM along the bottom" %>
      <figcaption>Capture</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Gesture</th><th>On a page</th><th>In a menu</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th>Tap the pad</th>
          <td>goes to the next page, or selects the next recording type on the capture page</td>
          <td>moves to the next row, or returns to the menu&rsquo;s page after the last row</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Touch the pad, 1&nbsp;s</th>
          <td>silences an active alarm, or returns to the radar if no alarm is active</td>
          <td>returns to the radar</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>One press of the button</th>
          <td>opens this page&rsquo;s menu, or rejects a confirmation request on the screen</td>
          <td>acts on the selected row, with each further press changing its value again</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Two presses, under 0.6&nbsp;s apart</th>
          <td colspan="2">accept a confirmation request on the screen, start or stop a recording on the capture page, and have no effect elsewhere</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Hold the button, 2&nbsp;s</th>
          <td colspan="2">switches the device off</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>The same hold, finger on the pad</th>
          <td colspan="2">switches it off and leaves the screen blank, for storage</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

